(def map-page "(map items function)\n\nReturns an iterator over a function's result for each item.\n\nIt is lazy: the function runs when a later call reads the item. A vector or\na map passes as its `iter`. A keyword such as `:age` reads that field.")
(def reduce-page "(reduce items step)\n\nCombines the items into one value with a function of two arguments.\n\n`step` takes the value so far and the next item. The first item starts the\nvalue, and the call returns an `option`, `none` for no items.\n\n`(reduce items initial step)` starts from `initial` and returns the value\nitself. A vector or a map passes as its `iter`. Its items are borrows, so\nthe first form takes `(copied items)` for a step such as `+`.")
(def count-page "(count items)\n\nReturns the number of items of an iterator as a `usize`.\n\n`(count (iter collection))` emits the collection's `len`, and any other call\nruns through the items. A vector or a map passes as its `iter`.")
(def max-page "(max items)\n\nReturns the largest item as an `option`.\n\nIt returns `none` for no items, and the last of equal items. The items\nimplement `ord`, so a float is an error. A vector or a map passes as its\n`iter`.")
